/P 96 0 R
/E (Maritime chokepoints have evolved and play a key role in global trade, and are essential for accessing ports. Due to their locations, chokepoints notably hold a lot of traffic and are often completely congested. Chokepoints, because of their high volumes of ships, struggle with vulnerability to conflicts, tensions, and disruptions. Countries and governments controlling global chokepoints have failed to respond to and treat disputes.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
