/E (Global trade today remains highly dependent on a small number of  maritime chokepoints, most notably the Suez Canal, Panama Canal, Strait of Hormuz, and the Strait of Malacca. A key issue in the current global situations Is the question of who should control major shipping chokepoints and to what extent International oversight Is necessary. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
